ant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA, KOJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKAMATSU MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HARA KATSUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKAMATSU, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARA, KATSUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a compound represented by general formula [7], wherein R&lt;1&gt; represents optionally substituted cycloalkyl, optionally substituted aryl, or optionally substituted heterocycle; R&lt;2&gt; represents lower alkyl or halogenated lower alkyl; and R&lt;3&gt; represents halogeno or hydrogen. The process comprises reacting a compound [1] with thionyl chloride to obtain a compound [2] and converting it to the target compound [7] through an intermediate [5]. It is capable of yielding the compound [7] in high yield and is utilizable for industrial production.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production d'un composé représenté par la formule générale [7] dans laquelle R&lt;1&gt; représente cycloalkyle éventuellement substitué, aryle éventuellement substitué ou hétérocycle éventuellement substitué; R&lt;2&gt; représente alkyle inférieur ou alkyle inférieur halogéné; et R&lt;3&gt; représente halogéno ou hydrogène. Le procédé de l'invention consiste à faire réagir un composé [1] avec du chlorure de thionyle de manière qu'un composé [2] soit obtenu et à le convertir en composé cible [7] en passant par un intermédiaire [5]. Ledit procédé permet la production dudit composé [7] avec un rendement élevé et peut être utilisé pour la production industrielle.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>